# Windows batch files: cmd.exe REQUIRES CRLF line endings (LF-only .bat files
# mis-parse multi-line if/for blocks -> "was unexpected at this time" crashes).
# text eol=crlf normalizes checkins to LF in the repo and materializes CRLF on
# every checkout, ZIP export and file copy, so future LF-only content edits can
# never be delivered to cmd.exe without CRLF again (the a61f966 regression
# class). The windows-smoke CI step is the behavioral guard for this.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
